# ============================================================================
# SimpleHost — sample hosts file
# ============================================================================
# A ready-made, self-contained hosts file for exercising SimpleHost end to end
# without touching your real system hosts file. Point the app at it with the
# "--hosts-file <path>" argument or the SIMPLEHOST_HOSTS_FILE environment
# variable (see the README). A custom file like this one is written WITHOUT
# administrator elevation, so it is safe to edit and re-run as often as you like.
#
# The layout below exercises every shape SimpleHost understands: uncategorized
# entries, "# [SimpleHost:Category] <Name>" markers, trailing inline "#"
# comments, and a disabled (commented-out) entry that is kept but does not
# resolve. Plain comment lines like these are ignored by the app.
# ============================================================================

# Entries above the first category marker belong to the "No category" group,
# which SimpleHost always pins to the top of the list.
127.0.0.1        localhost
::1              localhost                 # IPv6 loopback

# [SimpleHost:Category] Local development
127.0.0.1        api.myapp.test            # backend API
127.0.0.1        web.myapp.test            # local frontend
127.0.0.1        admin.myapp.test
# 127.0.0.1      staging.myapp.test        # disabled: not deployed locally yet

# [SimpleHost:Category] Ad blocking
0.0.0.0          ads.example.com
0.0.0.0          tracker.example.net       # third-party analytics beacon

# [SimpleHost:Category] Staging
203.0.113.10     app.staging.example.com   # RFC 5737 documentation address
203.0.113.11     api.staging.example.com
